course: dictionary
lesson: 14132
title: Minimalist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A minimalist thing is very simple. It uses as few things, shapes or decorations as possible. «The room had a minimalist look: one white chair, one plain table and nothing on the walls.» The clue is in the list: only a few things, and nothing extra.
explain: Minimalist can also be a noun. A minimalist can be an artist, designer or composer who works in the style of minimalism, or a person who chooses to own very few possessions. «Ben is a minimalist: all his belongings fit in one small box.» Here Ben is a person, not a thing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "very simple, with few things" in place of minimalist. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Minimalist (adjective) means very simple, using as few things, shapes or decorations as possible.
fact: «Minimalist design» means design that uses only what is needed.
fact: «Minimalist living» means choosing to own very few possessions.
fact: A minimalist can be an artist, designer or composer, or a person who lives with very few things.
fact: A minimalist packer brings a tiny bag.
exercise: «The hotel room was minimalist: a bed, a lamp and nothing else.» What does minimalist mean? | *Very simple, with as few things as possible | Very old and dusty | Full of bright colours and patterns | Noisy and crowded
exercise: «Ben owns only ten things and gives the rest away. He is a minimalist.» What is a minimalist in this sentence? | A loud musician | A very large family | *A person who chooses to own very few things | A shop that sells furniture
exercise: «Her logo is minimalist: one small circle and one line.» What does the logo use? | Lots of bright shapes | *Only what is needed | Gold letters and pictures | Every colour in the paint box
test: «The minimalist drawing had just three lines.» What does minimalist suggest? | Very expensive | Covered in glitter | Messy and busy | *Very simple, with as little as possible
test: «Anya, a minimalist designer, makes posters with only one word.» What is a minimalist designer? | *An artist or designer who works in the style of minimalism | A teacher of maths | A pupil who never speaks | A cook who makes cakes
exam: «Tom is a minimalist packer: his whole trip fits in one tiny bag.» Which phrase best matches minimalist packer? | Someone who packs in the dark | Someone who brings a huge suitcase | Someone who forgets their bag | *Someone who brings very few things
